# Confetti Cannon, by Claude Fable 5.2, MiMo v2.6 Pro and SZ. An original peak-time electro-house track for the
# Techno style, in G major: brighter and sillier than the other Techno originals. One two-bar riff
# carries it. The call climbs root-3-5-6 in a 3+3+2 bounce; the answer jumps to the octave, leaves a
# hole, and falls back. The tune opens sung: the vocal sings the riff an octave up over a bare kick
# pulse, the beat joins under it, and the vocal hands the tune to the acid lead at the tease. It sits
# low (every root is between C3 and G3) on the acid lead, doubled in fuzz (inst=fuzz-lead) in the
# full sections, over a 909, a sub that only ever plays off the kick, off-beat stabs just above the
# riff, and an open root-and-fifth dark pad. The chopped wordless vocal (inst=vox-lead) answers in
# the riff's hole in the drops.
#
# The loop is G - Em - C - D, two bars a chord; the riff's answer bar adds the 6th (the 7th on Em).
# The second breakdown and the last 16 bars of the final drop turn it around into a rising
# C - D - Em - G (the lift), where the vocal sings one long climbing line. Both builds sit on C
# then D. Generated by tools/arranger/confetti-cannon.mjs.
# chords: G G6 Em Em7 C C6 D D6
# chords @65: C C C C D D D D
# chords @73: G G6 Em Em7 C C6 D D6
# chords @89: C C6 D D6 Em Em7 G G6
# chords @97: C C C C D D D D
# chords @105: G G6 Em Em7 C C6 D D6
# chords @121: C C6 D D6 Em Em7 G G6
# chords @137: G G6 Em Em7 C C6 D D6
#
# Form 1-8: the vocal sings the riff over a bare kick pulse
# Form 9-16: the beat and sub join under the vocal
# Form 17-24: the vocal hands the tune to the riff: only its call, quiet
# Form 25-32: the whole riff, louder every two bars; the pad and claps join
# Form 33-40: first groove: riff, off-beat stabs, claps, 16th hats
# Form 41-48: first groove: the fuzz double joins
# Form 49-56: breakdown 1: the kick drops; the pad and a quiet riff carry
# Form 57-64: breakdown 1: the vocal chop, a held sub and soft hats
# Form 65-72: build 1: a snare roll (quarters, eighths, sixteenths) and a riser over C then D
# Form 73-80: drop 1: everything
# Form 81-88: drop 1: the vocal answers in the riff's hole
# Form 89-96: breakdown 2: the kick drops; the vocal sings a long line over a rising C-D-Em-G
# Form 97-104: build 2: a faster roll, the riser an octave up
# Form 105-112: final drop: a rolling sub, the vocal chops
# Form 113-120: final drop: the same, with the fill into the lift
# Form 121-128: final drop, the lift: the riff climbs C-D-Em-G under the long vocal line, ride cymbal
# Form 129-136: final drop, the lift: second pass
# Form 137-144: outro: the riff's call fades over drums, sub and stabs
# Form 145-152: outro: kick, hats and sub, then kick and hats for the mixer
#
# Human feel: the kick, sub and riff stay on the grid (a sequencer). The off-beat hats swing 8 to
# 14 ticks late and the 16th before each beat 12 to 20, the claps drag 8 to 16, the stabs land 12
# to 22 late, the vocal sits behind the beat, and every hat, clap and stab has its own velocity.
title: Confetti Cannon
composer: Claude Fable 5, MiMo v2.6 Pro & SZ
about: Peak-time electro house at 126 in G major: one bouncing bass riff on the acid lead, doubled in fuzz, over an off-beat sub and a 909, with a chopped vocal answering in the drops and a rising lift at the end.
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
style: techno
key: G major
tempo: 126
time: 4/4

